hv (gnu path): make Sun's aschk build and run on a Linux host.

aschk is a plain C program (a lex scanner and a hash table): it reads the assembler sources and
offsets.chk, and reports a memory access whose size or type does not match the field offsets.chk
names. Sun's Makefile.platform runs it before every link (`q: chkasm`). It runs no SPARC code, so the
gnu path can run it too, from source, as the sun path does. Two defects in it, both invisible on
Solaris and fatal under glibc:

  - aschk_main.c add_name_file(): `char typestr[4]` takes sscanf("%4s"), which writes five bytes (four
    characters and the terminator): one byte past the array, onto the stack.
  - aslex.c (and aslex.l, which it was made from) lex_only(), label `cleanup:`: the block that frees
    tok_left_ptr is there twice, one after the other: a double free, which glibc stops the process on.
    The second copy is meant for the right operand (tok_right_ptr, never freed otherwise: with the
    second copy left in, AddressSanitizer shows the right-hand names, read at the two get_token()
    calls after the '+', as the leak). It frees tok_right_ptr, under the same condition.
    That is a reading of the code, checked by running: no double free, and those leaks are gone.
    (A leak of the register after `store` is still there; a few kilobytes in a program that runs
    for a second.)

The scanner is the shipped aslex.c, not a fresh flex run: the build needs no flex. aslex.l carries the
same change so that the two stay the same text. Nothing else in the tool is changed. For the
unmodified hypervisor sources and the reference offsets.chk it reports nothing and exits 0; for an
offsets.chk with CONFIG_MEMSIZE's size changed from 8 to 4 it reports main.s:212 and main.s:1486 and
exits 1.

gnu path only; changes nothing in the product (aschk writes no file). Applied by
build/hv_reset/gnu/build.sh to a copy of src/hypervisor/src/support/aschk, never to src/.

--- a/aschk_main.c
+++ b/aschk_main.c
@@ -149,7 +149,7 @@
 {
 	FILE *fp;
 	char	linebuf[MAXLINE];
-	char	typestr[4];
+	char	typestr[8];
 	char	symname[MAXLINE];
 	int	offset, size;
 	int	linenum;
--- a/aslex.c
+++ b/aslex.c
@@ -2312,8 +2312,8 @@
 		if (tok_left == T_name || tok_left == T_register) {
 			free(tok_left_ptr);
 		}
-		if (tok_left == T_name || tok_left == T_register) {
-			free(tok_left_ptr);
+		if (tok_right == T_name || tok_right == T_register) {
+			free(tok_right_ptr);
 		}
 		goto swallow;
 
--- a/aslex.l
+++ b/aslex.l
@@ -415,8 +415,8 @@
 		if (tok_left == T_name || tok_left == T_register) {
 			free(tok_left_ptr);
 		}
-		if (tok_left == T_name || tok_left == T_register) {
-			free(tok_left_ptr);
+		if (tok_right == T_name || tok_right == T_register) {
+			free(tok_right_ptr);
 		}
 		goto swallow;
 
